A||||6||Gokart||Oil pan bolt...........washer?||||5||
Z||000000||Gokart||03-20-2000||07:02 AM||||My oil pan bolt has a metal washer around it but still leaks a little through the bolt. It's on there tight, but still leaks. Can anyone recommend maybe a neoprene or rubber washer to use instead that will stand up to the heat so I'm not leaking there anymore? TIA||||reg||5
Z||000001||fiero56||03-20-2000||08:24 AM||||The oil pan bolt on my Fiero has a rubber washer built into the head of the bolt. Works good, I assumed it was stock, might try a parts store or the Fiero Store.||||reg||1
Z||000002||deceler8||03-20-2000||02:09 PM||||I had the same problem after my last oil change...dripping from the plug.<P>So I went to Autozone and asked if they had an application for a drain plug gasket...and they did. Basically a ribbed nylon 1/2" washer.<P>Put it on and it works. No more drips. And cost about 45 cents.||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||03-20-2000||03:37 PM||||Those nylon washers work pretty good, I've put them on a number of my vehicles.||||reg||1
Z||000004||ka4nkf||03-20-2000||05:21 PM||||The nylon washer is great, i tried the coper washer and it leaked. i put the nylon washer on and no more leaks.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Gokart||03-20-2000||08:36 PM||||Thanks guys! Will pick up a nylon washer so I'll have it ready next time I do a change. Do I remove the steel washer on the bolt or just add the nylon washer to it?||||reg||14
Z||000006||theogre||03-20-2000||08:53 PM||||remove the old washer.............||||reg||1
